---
alwaysApply: true
---
When ever you try to execute a command do not prefix it wit a cd command to ensure you are in the correct directory. This will cause the command to fail.

For example, the following command will fail:
```bash
cd /Users/jasper/Work/fuzzyfilter/packages/fuzzyfilter && bun test src/fuzzy-filter.test.ts 
```

Instead, you should execute the command directly:
```bash
bun test src/fuzzy-filter.test.ts 
```